    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19-a1-a13">

                <pb facs="0078" n="36" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg36"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.</seg></opener>
                <head>[Official notice in the Gibraltar Chronicle of December 10, 1862.]</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">NOTICE.</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary’s Office</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Gibraltar,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-12-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 10, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>His excellency the <hi rendition="#small-caps">governor</hi> has received a
                    protest from the United States consul in this city against the sale of the
                    confederate steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Sumter</hi>, on the ground, as
                    stated by him, of her being a prize. No proof of this being the case has been
                    furnished, but the <hi rendition="#small-caps">governor</hi> deems it right to
                    notify this protest to the public.</p>
                <p>By command:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. FREELING, <hi rendition="#italic">Colonial
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
